{
  "slug": "llm-secure-patterns",
  "name": "Llm Secure Patterns",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Secure design patterns for Claude Code LLM applications: external content ingestion, endpoint hardening, output validation, system prompt design, and multi-agent action surface control. Maps to OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications 2025.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `agent-action-surface` (Use when designing or wiring up tool_use, function_calling, MCP servers, multi-agent chains, or calling multiple LLM providers (e.g.,…), `llm-endpoint-hardening` (Use when designing or building a web route (FastAPI, Flask, Express, or similar) that accepts user input and…), `output-validation` (Use when designing or implementing code where LLM responses are rendered as HTML or markup in a frontend,…), `report` (Generate OWASP LLM Top 10 security posture report from codebase annotations), `secure-external-ingestion` (Use when designing or implementing code that fetches URLs, scrapes pages, calls external APIs, parses PDFs/HTML from untrusted…), `system-prompt-design` (Use when designing, writing, editing, or reviewing system prompts for any LLM application — fire this skill during…)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install llm-secure-patterns@claude-community` from `wildblue-ai/llm-secure-patterns`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "hook": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
